class.description:
A [DataTable] holds rows and columns of data, for example the items of a game, the rows of a [CSV] file or the records of a JSON array. Each column is a [DataField] of [member schema]: its name, its [enum Variant.Type] and its rules. Cells are converted to the column type when they are set: text and numbers convert, as [code]"42"[/code] or [code]42.0[/code] in an [int] column.
Cells are stored per column (Structure of Arrays): an [int], [float], [String] or [bool] column is one packed array, any other type (and a column without a fixed type, [constant TYPE_NIL]) is an [Array]. [method get_column] returns that array without copying the cells, for fast reads in games.
A row does not need to have every cell. A cell that is not set is absent: [method has_cell] returns [code]false[/code], [method get_cell] returns [code]null[/code], and [method get_row] and [method to_records] leave its key out. So records with optional keys keep their shape in a round trip, and [code]null[/code] stays a value of its own in a column without a fixed type.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var table = DataTable.new()
table.add_column(&"id", TYPE_INT)
table.add_column(&"name", TYPE_STRING)
table.add_column(&"hp", TYPE_INT)
table.add_row({ "id": 1, "name": "Archer", "hp": 40 })
table.add_row({ "id": 2, "name": "Knight" })
table.set_cell(1, table.find_column(&"hp"), 55)

var hp_values = table.get_column(table.find_column(&"hp")) # PackedInt64Array(40, 55)
table.rows_inserted.connect(func(row, count): print("%d rows inserted at %d" % [count, row]))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var table = new DataTable();
table.AddColumn("id", Variant.Type.Int);
table.AddColumn("name", Variant.Type.String);
table.AddColumn("hp", Variant.Type.Int);
table.AddRow(new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "id", 1 }, { "name", "Archer" }, { "hp", 40 } });
table.AddRow(new Godot.Collections.Dictionary { { "id", 2 }, { "name", "Knight" } });
table.SetCell(1, table.FindColumn("hp"), 55);

long[] hpValues = table.GetColumn(table.FindColumn("hp")).AsInt64Array(); // [40, 55]
table.RowsInserted += (row, count) => GD.Print($"{count} rows inserted at {row}");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Signals:[/b] every change emits one of [signal cells_changed], [signal rows_inserted], [signal rows_removed] or [signal columns_changed], and then [signal Resource.changed]. A view connects to the specific signals to update only what changed.
[b]Columns and schema:[/b] the table creates its own [member schema]; assign a saved [DataSchema] to share the columns between tables. Changing the schema directly (adding, removing or retyping a [DataField]) updates the table: cells follow their field, or a field of the same name.
[b]Other storage:[/b] by default the cells live in memory. A script, a GDExtension or an engine subclass can override [method _get_row_count], [method _get_cell], [method _has_cell], [method _set_cell], [method _erase_cell], [method _insert_rows], [method _remove_rows], [method _insert_column] and [method _remove_column] to expose the data of another source, such as a file or a database, without copying it. Override all of them; the columns still come from [member schema].
[b]Conversion:[/b] [method create_from_records] and [method to_records] convert from and to an [Array] of [Dictionary] records (JSON, YAML, TOML), [method create_from_csv] and [method to_csv] from and to a [CSV] resource.
